course: dictionary
lesson: 12832
title: Enact: make it law, act it out, or carry it out
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Enact is a verb, a doing word. It has three meanings, so the words around it tell you which one is meant. Read the context first, then choose the meaning that fits.
explain: «Parliament enacted a new law about school bags.» The clue is law. To enact a law means to make it official, so everyone must follow it.
explain: «The class enacted the story of the Gingerbread Man on stage.» The clue is stage and story. To enact a scene means to act it out, like a play. Here enact means perform.
explain: «The leader enacted her plan to clean up the park.» The clue is plan. To enact a plan means to carry it out, to put it into action. Check your meaning by swapping in a simple word such as "carry out" or "act out" and seeing if the sentence still makes sense.
fact: Enact is a verb: enact, enacts, enacted, enacting.
fact: «Enact» means to make something official, especially a law, so it becomes law.
fact: «Enact» can also mean to act out a story or scene.
fact: «Enact» can mean to carry out a plan, which is a more formal use.
fact: Parliament enacts laws, children enact scenes in drama, and news reports can say a council has «enacted a new rule».
exercise: «The council enacted a new rule about bikes in the park.» What does enacted mean here? | Took all the bikes away | Painted the bikes | Rode very fast | *Made it official, so it became a rule
exercise: «The class enacted the story of the Three Little Pigs.» What does enacted mean here? | *Acted the story out | Forgot the story | Read it silently to themselves | Wrote the story down
exercise: In «She enacted her plan to build a treehouse», which word means the same as enacted? | Slept | Argued | Forgot | *Carried out
test: «Parliament enacts laws that everyone must follow.» Which meaning of enact is used here? | *Make a law official | Act out a scene | Ask a question | Paint a wall
test: «The actors enacted the battle on the stage.» What does enacted mean? | Counted the actors | Ran away from the battle | Painted the stage | *Acted out the battle
exam: «The mayor hopes to enact the plan next spring.» What does enact mean here? | Ask about | Eat | *Carry out | Cancel
